answer:
You are launching 12 shades of one lipstick formula that differ only in color. For this product line, you must file a single cosmetic product listing that includes all 12 shades because they share the same formulation and differ only in color.

The filing is required under FD&C Act § 607(c)(3)(B), which allows a single listing to include multiple cosmetic products with identical formulations that differ only in color, fragrance, or flavor. This provision specifically permits such a flexible submission for products differing solely by color [3].

You must file the product listing not later than 120 days after first marketing any shade of the lipstick in interstate commerce, as required under FD&C Act § 607(c)(2) [3]. 

The listing must include:  
- The facility registration number(s) where the products are manufactured or processed;  
- The name and contact number of the responsible person;  
- The name of each cosmetic product as it appears on the label (e.g., "Lipstick Shade 1", etc.);  
- The applicable cosmetic category (e.g., lip color);  
- A list of ingredients, including any fragrances or colors, identified by their name or common/usual name;  
- The product listing number assigned by the Secretary [3].

The responsible person may submit the product listing as part of a facility registration or separately, per FD&C Act § 607(c)(6) [3]. 

After the initial submission, any updates to the listing must be made annually, consistent with the requirement in FD&C Act § 607(c)(5), which mandates annual updates to content [3].

These provisions do not require separate listings for each shade. The fact that the products differ only in color is sufficient to treat them as a single listing under the flexible listing rule [3]. 

The available regulatory sources do not provide enough information to answer whether any additional FDA review or approval is required beyond the product listing submission, nor do they specify any restrictions on the use of the shade names or labeling details beyond what is required in the listing.
